r_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1748555952", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 25, "count": 1}]}, {"recommendationid": "212812168", "author": {"steamid": "76561199277867159", "personaname": "quibbelin", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199277867159/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 19, "playtime_forever": 573, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 345, "last_played": 1765559104, "avatar": "b10c3b2a6e9730965b6c9d7f45f2a2051197aed3"}, "language": "english", "review": "fun", "timestamp_created": 1765146890, "timestamp_updated": 1765146890, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1748555952", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "212811996", "author": {"steamid": "76561198039989738", "personaname": "addy", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/tfuiyh/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 34, "playtime_forever": 1057, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1057, "last_played": 1765145073, "avatar": "4f0782b994733a8caea1e688a5b9adbd28819484"}, "language": "english", "review": "I [i]really want to[/i] love Nightreign. I’m a huge Souls fan with countless runs across the series, and I own hundreds of roguelikes, so on paper this should be perfect for me. But something just doesn’t click.\n\nThe game throws you in fast and expects you to keep up. If you stop for even a moment to read new abilities or compare weapons, you’re either falling behind your teammates or losing levels because you didn’t rush to the next objective. The tutorial barely explains how the game actually works, so it’s easy to wander into bosses way above your level and lose both time and souls trying to recover.\n\nMeta progression is extremely limited for a roguelike. Each character has 3 rune slots, and those runes can roll up to 3 affixes, so your long-term progression is basically just 9 stat quirks. Some of them are cool, but it doesn’t change how limited it all feels. And because item drops are random, you can easily end up stuck with weapon types you don’t want, making some runs feel flat-out worse through no fault of your own.\n\nCommunication is another huge miss. Outside of simple map pings, there’s no text chat, no voice chat, nothing. If you’re solo-queuing, coordinating with random teammates is almost impossible.\n\nThere are great boss fights here, and moments that remind you why FromSoftware’s combat systems are so beloved. But getting to those moments means pushing through confusing itemization, a lack of build variety, shallow progression, and no real way to communicate.\n\nI want Nightreign to be amazing, but right now it’s unfortunately more frustrating than fun.", "timestamp_created": 1765146678, "timestamp_updated": 1765146678, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 46, "votes_funny": 4, "weighted_vote_score": "0.643423378467559814", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1748555952", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 16, "count": 1}, {"reaction_type": 19, "count": 1}, {"reaction_type": 3, "count": 1}]}, {"recommendationid": "212811445", "author": {"steamid": "76561198024396816", "personaname": "Ghost of a Dragon", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198024396816/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 7, "playtime_forever": 3175, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 2519, "last_played": 1771040403, "avatar": "79d3fe5839617eb83a9661071ed021dd56ac8a5b"}, "language": "english", "review": "This game is awesome and the DLC adds 